(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #130: the compiler can read a text literal for itself,
 and a text is a number only when the whole of it could be written as a
 number literal in Vox source. None of these could, so each cast could
 only ever fail.)

a number called count is 0.
Set count to "hello" as a number.
Set count to "12 apples" as a number.
Set count to "1.5x" as a number.
Set count to "" as a number.
Set count to "-" as a number.
Set count to "0x" as a number.
Set count to "0o8" as a number.
Set count to "0b2" as a number.
Set count to "--1" as a number.
Set count to "1-" as a number.
Set count to "7 " as a number.
Set count to " 7" as a number.
Set count to "+7" as a number.
Set count to "1e5" as a number.
Set count to "3." as a number.
Print count.
